# NO LONGER LOAD-BEARING — kept as a backstop, not as the defence.
#
# wrangler reads .assetsignore from inside the assets directory. That is now
# dist/ (see wrangler.jsonc), which tools/build.sh rebuilds from empty on every
# run and fills with site files only — so there is nothing left to exclude and
# this file is not consulted at all.
#
# It stays for one reason: if anyone ever points "assets.directory" back at "."
# the old failure returns instantly, and it returns silently. Publishing the
# repo root made the deploy surface "everything, minus whatever this file
# remembered", so anything new shipped BY DEFAULT — which is how tools/ (every
# build script, the command corpus, siteconf.py with both Search Console
# tokens) and a ~4,700-file Mermaid install ended up publicly fetchable, and
# why .git was the only thing anyone had thought to list.
#
# The real fix is the output directory. This is the seatbelt behind it.

.git
.git/**
.github
.github/**
.wrangler
.wrangler/**
node_modules
node_modules/**
.gitignore
wrangler.jsonc
wrangler.toml
CNAME
tools
tools/**
content
content/**
static
static/**
*.py
*.sh
__pycache__
__pycache__/**
.fontcache
.fontcache/**
